[node name="OptionButton" type="OptionButton" parent="." unique_id=1237191194]
z_index = 10
offset_left = 1079.0
offset_top = 691.0
offset_right = 1237.0
offset_bottom = 722.0
tooltip_text = "Fitness evolution across generations.

Mean fitness is the arithmetic mean of the fitness values of all 100
agents in a generation.

This mean includes the 5 renewed agents introduced by the current
reproduction methodology: 3 descendants produced by elite × new-random
crossovers and 2 fully random agents.

Best fitness is the highest individual fitness obtained in that
generation.

Higher values indicate better overall performance under the current
simulation's fitness function."
theme = SubResource("Theme_5bjn8")

[node name="OptionButton2" type="OptionButton" parent="." unique_id=525999736]
z_index = 10
offset_left = 1079.0
offset_top = 842.0
offset_right = 1237.0
offset_bottom = 873.0
tooltip_text = "Genetic diversity is the mean normalized Hamming distance between all
pairs of genomes in the main evolving population.

The 5 renewed agents introduced each generation are excluded from this
calculation: 3 descendants produced by elite × new-random crossovers
and 2 fully random agents.

For genomes g_i and g_j of length L, their normalized Hamming distance is

d(g_i,g_j) = (1/L) * sum_k [g_i(k) != g_j(k)].

The reported diversity is the mean of d(g_i,g_j) over all unordered
pairs of the remaining agents.

A value of 0 means all compared genomes are identical. A value of 1
means every compared pair differs at every gene position.

Equivalent percentage interpretation:
1      = 100% of gene digits differ on average
1e-1 = 10% differ on average
1e-2 = 1% differ on average
1e-3 = 0.1% differ on average
1e-4 = 0.01% differ on average
0      = 0% differ on average

These values are pairwise averages, so the implied number of differing
gene digits per pair does not need to be an integer."
mouse_filter = 1
theme = SubResource("Theme_qux5w")

[node name="Title2" type="Label" parent="." unique_id=1660812460]
offset_left = 35.0
offset_top = 547.0
offset_right = 360.0
offset_bottom = 581.0
tooltip_text = "This heatmap shows the relation between  
two selected genes and agent fitness.

Each axis represents one selected gene. 
Gene values are ordered using a
quaternary Gray code. Nearby positions 
therefore tend to represent small genetic 
changes.

Each cell contains the mean fitness
of all agents that fell into that bin.
Data from all generations in the
current simulation are accumulated.

The color scale is fixed from -1 to 1.
Bright pink cells have no samples yet.

Changing either gene selector rebuilds
the heatmap from the stored history.
"
mouse_filter = 1
theme = SubResource("Theme_sx4as")
theme_override_colors/font_color = Color(0.8862745, 0.15686275, 0.15686275, 1)
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 18
text = "Genetic x Fitness Landscape"

